bs/wm-contract/runs/F13-model-manifest-2026-09-15/redo/retrieval-index.tsv", :lines [1324 1324], :quote "social/verify-before-compose\t\t\tVerify Each Component Before Composing It With Others -> unknown/unknown: The event-protocol pattern (futon-theory/event-protocol) requires OBSERVE before PROPOSE_CLAIM and VERIFY before the next step; applying this same discipline to development means you cannot claim a namespace works (PROPOSE_CLAIM) without first loading it (OBSERVE) and checking its public API (VERIFY). Forward declarations are evidence that PROPOSE_CLAIM preceded OBSERVE.\tverify, each, component, before, composing, others, social, compose, event, protocol"}], :source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/social/verify-before-compose.flexiarg", :author "codex-27", :sha256 "7423336ec6e5e65c2be3423a3acab13dc96629d2376319937a3962cb34e2a59f", :clauses {:if {:source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/social/verify-before-compose.flexiarg", :lines [14 14], :quote "    Components are designed as coherent architectural units — a registry, a proof-tree forum, a bell/whistle protocol — and written to match a design specification."}, :however {:source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/social/verify-before-compose.flexiarg", :lines [17 17], :quote "    Code written to match a design document without incremental load-and-test accumulates latent errors (unresolved forward declarations, namespace ordering, type mismatches) that only surface when integration is attempted. At that point the debugging cost is multiplicative: each broken dependency interacts with every other, and the developer cannot tell whether a failure is in their code or in a dependency they assumed worked."}, :then {:source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/social/verify-before-compose.flexiarg", :lines [25 25], :quote "    Require each namespace to compile and load before adding the next dependency. Write a minimal smoke test (can I call each public function without exception?) before composing namespaces. Treat a forward-declaration fix as a bug report against the development process, not a normal commit."}}, :effect {"complete-per-node-suite-exists" true}, :guard [:and [:fact "components-built"] [:not [:fact "complete-per-node-suite-exists"]]], :pattern "social/verify-before-compose"} {:authority :documented-interpretation, :membership [{:source "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F13-model-manifest-2026-09-15/redo/retrieval-index.tsv", :lines [1323 1323], :quote "social/tension-before-code\t\t\tSpecify Invariants Before Writing the Code They Constrain -> unknown/unknown: The structural-tension-as-observation pattern (futon-theory) defines three detection criteria: structural irritation (recurring gaps), pre-symbolic pressure (repeated early failures), and trans-situational reappearance (same pattern across contexts). All five Agency invariant violations (A0-A5) exhibited all three criteria across two generations of code before they were named. The observation loop existed in theory; it was not running in practice. Writing tests first forces the loop to run.\tspecify, invariants, before, writing, code, constrain, social, tension, structural, observation"}], :source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/social/tension-before-code.flexiarg", :author "codex-27", :sha256 "b8ae831777287a1613c564781ff74c60958c89c509cbec427e131a72a2fff884", :clauses {:if {:source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/social/tension-before-code.flexiarg", :lines [14 14], :quote "    The system is built feature-first — bells, pages, registries, kick endpoints, session tracking — with correctness properties assumed to hold implicitly through careful coding."}, :however {:source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/social/tension-before-code.flexiarg", :lines [17 17], :quote "    Without explicit invariants specified upfront, each successive generation discovers violations that were present from the start. The \"rebuild\" that fixes them is a confession that retroactively names what should have been preconditions. This turns development into an unbounded cycle: build features -> discover violations -> confess invariants -> rebuild -> discover new violations. Agency went through three generations of this cycle before achieving invariant coverage."}, :then {:source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/social/tension-before-code.flexiarg", :lines [25 25], :quote "    Write invariant proof tests first, as failing tests that define the boundary conditions. Derive the implementation from what the tests require. Treat any invariant discovered during implementation (rather than before it) as a tension observation: record it, but also ask why the structural-tension-as-observation loop did not detect it earlier."}}, :effect {"complete-per-node-suite-exists" true}, :guard [:and [:fact "node-spec-map-exists"] [:not [:fact "complete-per-node-suite-exists"]]], :pattern "social/tension-before-code"} {:authority :documented-interpretation, :membership [{:source "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F13-model-manifest-2026-09-15/redo/new-index-row.patch", :lines [7 7], :quote "+coordination/bind-promotion-to-post-repair-replay\tlili\t予\tBind Promotion to Post-Repair Replay -> lili/e: Keep repaired certificates pending until independent replay matches the repaired revision.\trepair, replay, promotion, certificate, revision, independent, pending"}], :source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/coordination/bind-promotion-to-post-repair-replay.flexiarg", :author "codex-27", :sha256 "e7703a5b23a26eb9cd8790a4181b739a8beb73645ffb8d9ac755e79b9fc4f0d7", :clauses {:if {:source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/coordination/bind-promotion-to-post-repair-replay.flexiarg", :lines [14 14], :quote "    Fixes for the witnessed defects have landed, but no qualifying independent replay receipt for the repaired revision has been recorded."}, :however {:source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/coordination/bind-promotion-to-post-repair-replay.flexiarg", :lines [16 16], :quote "    Passing regression tests establishes the repairs' local checks, not the previously refused certificate. A request is not a completed replay, and a receipt for another revision cannot discharge this obligation."}, :then {:source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/coordination/bind-promotion-to-post-repair-replay.flexiarg", :lines [18 18], :quote "    Keep the certificate pending and record an independent replay request naming the repaired revision and the rejected controls. Reuse an already recorded matching request rather than claiming a new replay. Promote only after a successful independent receipt matches that revision and those controls; otherwise retain a typed pending or failed finding."}}, :effect {"replay-request-recorded" true, "pending-status-recorded" true}, :guard [:and [:fact "regression-fixes-landed"] [:not [:fact "independent-replay-confirmed"]]], :pattern "coordination/bind-promotion-to-post-repair-replay"}], :genesis [{:pattern "coordination/bind-promotion-to-post-repair-replay", :source "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/coordination/bind-promotion-to-post-repair-replay.flexiarg", :index-source "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F13-model-manifest-2026-09-15/redo/retrieval-index.tsv", :commit "cc231bf6f479c0dd87629edeca87b7c7dd973909", :gap "Retrieved independent-validation pattern omits explicit post-repair revision matching and request-versus-completion distinction."}], :target {:id "M-zaif-harness-v1", :kind :mission, :action {:type :advance-mission, :target "M-zaif-harness-v1"}, :source "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/missions/M-zaif-harness-v1.md", :citations [{:source "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/missions/M-zaif-harness-v1.md", :lines [3 9], :quote "**Date:** 2026-09-02\n**Status:** OPEN — HEAD through VERIFY drafted; INSTANTIATE runs as wm-contract U rows.\n**Owner:** claude-1. Driver: Joe.\n**Home:** futon2/holes/ (successor edition to `M-zaif-harness.md`, 2026-07-11, which stays\nthe v0 record; this document does not rewrite it).\n**Lifecycle:** `futon4/holes/missi